WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.280
- [Narrator] China is reopening again

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.890
after years of COVID-19 restrictions.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.180
The country also announced

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.860
it will drop quarantine requirements

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.690
for international travelers.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.520
- This reopening for China has been

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.840
the biggest step they've taken

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.390
after almost three years of isolation.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.710
- [Narrator] In response, the US

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.690
and several other countries want travelers

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:22.980
from China to show a negative
COVID-19 test before entering.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.160
That's because China is facing
a huge wave of infections.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.620
Hospitals are overcrowded
and major outbreaks

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.810
are spreading across the country.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.430
So, three years into the pandemic,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.010
we'll see a return of travel restrictions.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.363
Here's what that means.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.510
China has largely been
isolated from the rest

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.354
of the world since 2020,

00:00:41.354 --> 00:00:44.100
(Protestors chanting in Chinese)

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.990
but following nationwide protests

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.640
and a steep economic slide,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.880
Beijing removed almost all
of its testing, lockdown,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.720
and quarantine measures,
including on international travel.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.760
Starting January 8th, people traveling

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.150
to China will only need to
provide a negative COVID-19 test

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.340
within 48 hours of arrival.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.960
- This is a big change
from the last couple

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.210
of years when it's been 14,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.230
or 21 days even, of mandatory
centralized quarantine.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.780
- [Narrator] But COVID-19
cases began to surge soon

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.480
after restrictions were
lifted and many pharmacies

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.090
in major cities ran low on medication.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.700
Scientists say it's easy
for existing variants

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.460
of the virus, like
Omicron, to spread quickly

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.000
in a place where few people
had been previously infected.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.880
- We've seen the virus
spread like wildfire

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.020
across the country.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.320
You're seeing hospitals
often get inundated

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.110
with COVID patients,
particularly the elderly,

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.280
and then, you are also seeing,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.110
like, factory owners complaining

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.960
because many of their workers
have been sick with COVID

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.750
and it spread so quickly
that it very often is like 30

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.930
or 40% of their workforce out at one time.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.310
- [Narrator] For travelers from China,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.823
that means new challenges when
flying to other countries.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.270
The US, India, Italy, and Japan were some

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.120
of the countries that immediately
imposed new restrictions

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.043
for incoming travelers from China.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.530
US health officials said China

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.470
was providing limited data on the surge.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.730
- [Liza] I think what governments

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.060
and also other health officials
are concerned about is

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.080
that China might not be able
to control the spread of COVID

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.380
and from there, there
might be new variants.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.170
- After reintroducing
COVID testing on arrival,

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.870
Italian officials said more
than half of the passengers

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.140
on one of the first flights
from China tested positive.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.540
The Prime Minister wants mandatory tests

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.477
across the European Union.

00:02:32.477 --> 00:02:36.060
(Giorgia speaking Italian)

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.360
China has responded by
calling for other countries

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.275
to prioritize the economic
benefits of travel.

00:02:45.275 --> 00:02:48.608
(Wang speaking Chinese)

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.640
While countries continue to
monitor for developments,

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.930
more restrictions may be

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.540
in store for travelers coming from China.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.670
- I think these travel
restrictions are a road bump,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.490
but not a wall, because
people have been locked down

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.500
in China for almost three years.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.770
There's a huge pent up
demand for travel globally.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.120
A day after, China said

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.850
that they would lift
the border restrictions.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.410
We saw trip.com, which is a
huge travel provider in China.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.020
They were saying outbound
travel bookings were up

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.500
almost 300% because there
was so much pent up demand.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.773
I just don't see it as a
very big restriction at all.

